# Liga

Billiards club ratings + handicapped double-elim tournaments. Intent:
`docs/intent/liga.md`. Direction: `docs/ideas/liga.md`. Map: `docs/liga/map.md`.

## Stack

- JVM: ZIO HTTP (`liga`), Glicko2, append-only tournament JSON replay
- Shared: `liga-common` (cross JVM/JS) — handicap, race-to scopes, types
- UI: Laminar Scala.js (`liga-js`) — director + audience SPAs
- CLI: `atbp liga` (leaderboard / handicap / serve)

## Commands

```bash
sbt --client "liga/compile"
sbt --client "liga/test"
sbt --client "liga-js/test"
sbt --client "liga/testOnly *Handicap*"
sbt --client "liga/testOnly *WaitTiming*"
sbt --client "liga-js/testOnly *BracketLayout*"
sbt --client fixup
sbt run   # no --client — verify serve starts
```

## Conventions

- Period files (`.liga`) are source of truth; never mutate completed periods
- Tournament state = append-only event dir; resume via replay
- Ratings freeze at period start; Glicko2 only on period complete
- Handicaps are suggestions until match start, then locked
- Race-to is per scope (WB/LB/GF rounds), not per match
- Director and audience are separate URLs/SPAs
- Wait/Done Instants are API-only projections (`MatchWaitTiming` →
  `waitStartedAt` / `completedAt`); never extend domain `BracketMatch`, never
  use `MatchReady.at` as wait start
- Director Ready strip via `BracketLayout.directorGroupMatches`; audience stays
  on `groupMatches` (do not parameterize the shared helper for the strip)

## Boundaries

- No auth, multi-tournament concurrency, cloud hosting, or mobile apps (v1)
- No in-period rating drift; no WebSockets (audience polls)
- Shared domain math lives in `liga-common`, not duplicated in `liga-js`
- Follow existing Laminar patterns in `liga-js/.../director/`
- No rest thresholds, colors-as-rules, auto-call, or audience list changes for
  wait indicators (see `SPEC.md` / `docs/intent/td-match-wait-indicators.md`)
